# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# air file
app/tmp

# env file
.env

# node
node_modules
/frontend/dist

# local env files
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Log files
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Editor directories and files
.idea
.vscode
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.DS_Store
.neon

# Vercel CLI — `vercel link` / `vercel pull` write the linked project id
# and the pulled production env here. Local state, never committed.
.vercel
.env*

# Playwright visual tests — reports and diffs are per-run artifacts. The
# baselines themselves (frontend/tests/visual/__screenshots__) are committed:
# they are the assertion.
/frontend/test-results
/frontend/playwright-report
/frontend/blob-report

# Perf load-test reports (frontend/loadtest/run.js) — one JSON+txt pair per
# run, against a moving target (production), never meant to be committed.
/frontend/loadtest/reports

# CodeGraph index — a ~10MB SQLite graph of this repo plus the indexing
# daemon's pid/socket/log, rebuilt from the source on demand and entirely
# per-developer. Nothing in it is authored, it churns on every edit, and
# whether to index at all is each developer's own choice.
/.codegraph

# Claude Code agent worktrees — throwaway checkouts an agent creates to work
# on an isolated copy of the tree, plus whatever build output it leaves
# behind (a stray node_modules/package-lock.json outlives the worktree once
# `git worktree remove` has detached it). Already excluded on this machine by
# .git/info/exclude, which the agent harness writes — but that file is local
# to one clone and never travels, so the rule is restated here to hold for
# every checkout of this repo.
/.claude/worktrees

# Claude Code per-developer settings — `settings.local.json` is the local
# half of the agent's config (today: a personal list of pre-approved tool
# permissions), deliberately distinct from a shared `.claude/settings.json`,
# which is not ignored and can be committed if this project ever wants one.
# Currently ignored only by a *global* gitignore on one machine, so the same
# reasoning as .claude/worktrees above applies: restated here to hold for
# every checkout rather than for whoever happens to have that global config.
/.claude/settings.local.json
